 Governor Ashby's base case is one 25bp cut, to 4.25%. She also said markets \"may be getting ahead of themselves.\"\n- **Multiple risk:** The factsheet says a 50bp lower policy path lifts the basket P/E by about 1.5 points. If the market moves from pricing 50bp of cuts to the CMA's 25bp, that is about 0.75 points of P/E lost. That takes the weighted forward P/E from 19x to roughly 18.25x. I'm assuming the 19x already reflects the market-implied path, which the sources don't confirm.\n- **Earnings:** Consensus expects 2027 EPS growth of 14%, driven by backlog conversion at Voltaris and Tarnwell. Estimates rose 3% over the past quarter.\n- **Net effect:** 1.14 × 18.25 / 19 ≈ 1.095, so about +9% implied price upside even after the multiple compresses.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- The result depends on the 14% EPS growth being delivered. If it falls short, the cushion shrinks.\n- If the CMA cut nothing, the multiple loss would be larger, about 1.5 points on the same rule.\n- The P/E sensitivity is a historical average, not a guarantee.\n- I didn't look at the Jan-2028 implied-vol series.","ttft_ms":2382,"type":"result","duration_ms":31073,"uuid":"cda690d3-d7e2-4f58-9ae8-54d338dbc0a5","ttft_stream_ms":1281,"time_to_request_ms":233,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":19,"system_prompt":22,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":11,"input_attachments":50,"input_hooks":12,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":5,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":23,"init_frame_send":8,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":13,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":7,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":29,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":10,"message_normalization":5,"client_creation":4,"request_build":9},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":73,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":84,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":171,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":97,"process_rss_mib_result":195,"process_anon_mib_result":113,"proce